```css
.toast {
  transition: transform 200ms cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1), opacity 200ms cubic-bezier(0.23, 1, 0.32, 1);
}
.toast[data-state="closing"] {
  transform: translateY(16px);
  opacity: 0;
}
```

I used an ease-out curve so the toast responds the moment it is dismissed.

```css
@media (prefers-reduced-motion: no-preference) {
  .toast[data-state="closing"] {
    transition: transform 220ms ease-in, opacity 220ms ease-in;
    transform: translateY(24px);
    opacity: 0;
  }
}
```

You asked for it to accelerate as it falls away, so the exit uses `ease-in`. The trade-off: ease-in starts slow, so the first frames after the dismiss barely move and can read as lag.

